        <txttip left="304" top="312" right="346" bottom="329" content="Trunk" fontname="Consolas" fontstyle="0" editsize="100" txtcolor="-16777216" txtbkcolor="-7278960" charset="1" />
        <txttip left="19" top="12" right="661" bottom="97" content="Scenario:&#x0D;&#x0A;As a network administrator of an existing enterprise network, it has been requested that the &#x0D;&#x0A;connections between the switches be used more effectively by preparing the switches to support &#x0D;&#x0A;link aggregation before establishing manual link aggregation, for which the media between the &#x0D;&#x0A;switches are to be configured as member links.&#x0D;&#x0A;" fontname="Consolas" fontstyle="0" editsize="90" txtcolor="-16777216" txtbkcolor="-7278960" charset="1" />
        <txttip left="19" top="109" right="604" bottom="219" content="Learning Objectives&#x0D;&#x0A;As part of this lab section, you are expected to achieve the following tasks:&#x0D;&#x0A;1.Manually set the line rate and duplex mode on an interface.&#x0D;&#x0A;2.Configuration of manual mode link aggregation.&#x0D;&#x0A;3.Configuration of link aggregation using static LACP mode.&#x0D;&#x0A;4.Management of the priority of interfaces in static LACP mode.&#x0D;&#x0A;" fontname="Consolas" fontstyle="0" editsize="100" txtcolor="-16777216" txtbkcolor="-7278960" charset="1" />
    </txttips>
